     "page": 1,
     "text": "Bennett and Sons Clinic \nDr. Andrea Cordova \nRe: Jennifer Jimenez (DOB 02/01/1981) \n\nFebruary 02, 2026: \nJennifer Jimenez presented to the clinic today with concerns related to her Peripheral arterial disease and aortic aneurysm. The patient's blood pressure was recorded at 133/80, and her weight was 169 pounds. Upon examination, she appeared to be doing well. She continues to monitor her condition closely and adheres to the treatment plan. Her aortic aneurysm, which is of the AAA type and measures 4 cm, is currently being managed conservatively without surgical intervention. The patient has no complaints, and her overall condition remains stable.\n\nSeptember 06, 2025: \nJennifer returned for a follow-up regarding her Peripheral arterial disease and aortic aneurysm. Her blood pressure was 145/89, and she weighed 178 pounds. She continues to do well without significant issues. Her eGFR remains at 52, indicating stable kidney function within the context of her Polycystic kidney disease. No new symptoms were reported, and her aortic aneurysm continues to be monitored. She has been advised to maintain regular follow-ups to ensure her condition is managed effectively.\n\nApril 10, 2025: \nJennifer was seen today for a medication refill and follow-up of her medical conditions. Her blood pressure was 137/89, and she weighed 175 pounds. Jennifer has been diagnosed with Polycystic kidney disease, for which her eGFR is 52. She also has a Peripheral arterial disease with an aortic aneurysm (AAA) that measures 4 cm. The patient reports no new symptoms and continues to manage her conditions well. She is compliant with her medications, which include latanoprost 0.005% for her glaucoma and metronidazole topical 1% for her rosacea.\n\nNovember 12, 2024: \nJennifer visited for a follow-up on her Polycystic kidney disease. Her blood pressure was 142/81, and she weighed 169 pounds. Her condition remains stable with an eGFR of 52. Additionally, her Peripheral arterial disease and aneurysm (AAA; 4 cm) are being without complications. She reports no new issues and continues to do well. Her glaucoma is controlled with latanoprost 0.005%, and her rosacea is managed with metronidazole topical 1%. She remains compliant with her medication regimen.\n\nJune 16, 2024: \nJennifer was seen for follow-up of her Polycystic kidney disease. Her blood pressure was 135/83, and she weighed 181 pounds. She is doing well with no new complaints. Her eGFR remains at S2, indicating stable kidney function. Her aortic aneurysm, which measures 4 cm, is being monitored regularly. Jennifer"
    },
